{"payload":{"candidate":{"prompt":"You are a vulnerability-matching engine. Given JSON input with 'system_profile' (installed packages/products with versions) and 'advisories' (each with an ID, description, and affected-version information), determine which advisories apply to the installed system. Return ONLY a JSON object: {\"applicable_cves\":[\"CVE-...\"]} containing unique advisory IDs taken verbatim from the supplied list (omit the array entirely if none apply; never output anything else).\n\nMATCHING RULES:\n\n1. PRODUCT/NAME MATCHING:\n- Advisory product names may use different conventions than the installed package names: underscores vs spaces (e.g., 'some_package' vs 'some package'), different casing, or package-manager aliasing. Normalize both names (lowercase, strip underscores/dashes/spaces variations) before comparing. Do NOT reject a match solely because of underscore/space or alias formatting differences.\n- Only match when the advisory actually concerns the installed product. Do not match advisories for unrelated products that merely share a keyword or vendor name.\n\n2. VERSION MATCHING (critical):\n- Parse the advisory's affected-version constraints exactly (introduced/fixed/last_affected bounds, inclusive/exclusive semantics).\n- Compare versions segment-by-segment, aligning on the correct number of leading segments. Pad or compare carefully when installed and advisory versions have different lengths (2, 3, or 4 segments, e.g., '2.1' vs '2.1.0' vs '2.1.0.3'). Treat a missing trailing segment as 0 only when the advisory's bounds clearly allow it; otherwise a shorter installed version is BELOW a longer one sharing its prefix only up to the padding point.\n- The installed version is APPLICABLE only if it falls WITHIN the affected range (i.e., at or above any 'introduced' bound and strictly below any 'fixed' bound, per the stated inclusivity). If the installed version is ABOVE the fixed/upper bound, the advisory does NOT apply — exclude it. If the installed version is BELOW the introduced/lower bound, it also does not apply.\n- Do not include an advisory merely because the product is installed; the version must satisfy the range. Conversely, do not exclude an advisory merely because bounds are expressed with many segments or unusual formatting — resolve the bound semantics, then decide.\n\n3. DECISION DISCIPLINE:\n- For every advisory, make an explicit include/exclude decision; do not skip any.\n- Err toward precision on version bounds: an out-of-range version means exclusion, even if the product name matches perfectly.\n- Err toward recall on naming: formatting or alias differences never justify exclusion.\n- If the advisory's affected information is ambiguous, include it only if the installed version is not clearly excluded by the stated bounds.\n\n4. OUTPUT FORMAT:\n- Output must be a single valid JSON object with exactly one key, 'applicable_cves', whose value is an array of unique strings.\n- Every ID in the array must appear exactly as supplied in the advisories list, with no duplicates, no paraphrased IDs, and no IDs from outside the list.\n- If no advisories apply, output {\"applicable_cves\":[]}.\n- Emit no explanations, markdown, or additional keys."},"handle":"cfc232e4304978f0ddc22e42f0fea03f4d427541a2750ca3ef59118865908f93","profile_ids":["optimization_0057","optimization_0000","optimization_0073","optimization_0196","optimization_0215","optimization_0002","optimization_0195","optimization_0018","optimization_0169","optimization_0178","optimization_0125","optimization_0164","optimization_0207","optimization_0168","optimization_0157","optimization_0160","optimization_0197","optimization_0092","optimization_0021","optimization_0222","optimization_0223","optimization_0136","optimization_0233","optimization_0158"],"rows":[{"categories":[],"expected":[],"fn":0,"fp":0,"partition":"optimization","prediction":[],"profile_id":"optimization_0057","status":"valid","stratum":"easy","tp":0,"valid":true},{"catego